-- title:
--   Reducedness mod p of the two chart rings of X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 1$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume $p \mid M$, $p^{2} \nmid M$, and that $H$ contains every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is $1$. Let $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of the matrices of $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose associated unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ (the class of the lower-right entry) lies in $H$, and let $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the set `intFormRatiosC ℚ Γ` of ratios of integral $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma$. Assume further that the series $j =$ `jqModC ℚ` $= q^{-1}\,(\text{integral power series})$ lies in the corresponding field for $\Gamma = \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, so that it defines an element `jAt Γ hj` of $F$. Write $R$ for the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, and let $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, resp. $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$, be the subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over $R[j]$, resp. over $R[j^{-1}]$. The conclusion is that both quotients $A_{\mathrm{fin}}/(p)$ and $A_{\mathrm{inf}}/(p)$, by the ideal generated by the image of the natural number $p$, are reduced rings.
--
--   The two rings are the affine charts of the normal two-chart model over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ of the modular curve $X_H(M)$; the assertion is the reducedness of their fibres over $p$, which for $p \parallel M$ and $H$ containing the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is the Deligne–Rapoport description of the fibre at $p$ as two copies of the curve in characteristic $p$ of level prime to $p$, crossing at the supersingular points. It feeds the chart-level analysis of that fibre, in particular the counting of minimal primes above $p$ and the construction of retractions to Laurent series used in the Deligne–Rapoport property bundle.
